    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 the two cited review runs resolve in the delivered ledger with reviewed heads matching their ids (s62 at 3897f62ee788, s64 at 7126b33f3e3b), and \u00a762/\u00a764 resolve as sections.",
    "done_when": "a finding \u2014 \u00a769's negative control is conditional (\"fails if the recording ignores the arms\") and is not reproducible at any revision.",
    "evidence_paths": "pass \u2014 both nodes place their base and head gate logs under the run's own directory, which survives the run.",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 the new test file names describe the mechanism (test_a_hand_*_completed_arms, test_a_held_plans_reason_survives_an_unweighed_pass) with no plan label, stage name or ticket number.",
    "reasoning": "a finding \u2014 \u00a770's deliverable prescribes a shared implementation (\"One rule decides \u2026 read by both the reflex and the obligations view\") where the reviewable fact is that the two views agree on which requests are held.",
    "single_goal": "a finding \u2014 \u00a770 carries three independent deliverables (reason survives an unweighed pass; one shared held-request rule; coverage and cap read once per pass) behind a single control covering only the first.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 \u00a769 declares its wait on \u00a762 and \u00a770 on \u00a764, each section builds on exactly that predecessor, and both ids appear in the open followup and in \u00a710's wait list."
